                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Experienced on the Meta Quest 2[/h1]\n\nYou can view my gameplay & early impressions here: https://youtu.be/Sm9mYZf_gf4\n\nThis is a cute, family friendly collection of online multiplayer pvp games that is perfect for families with kids. Even better, it's not currently heavily monetized. I only saw a season pass for cosmetic items (you get free ones too). On the downside though, I didn't see anybody online. You can technically play single-player, but it's not really fun to play it that way. However, if you have friends online with VR and you're looking for a family friendly set of PvP games, then I could easily recommend this game for you.\n\nThe main draw is the locomotion method. It's sort of like arm swing, but more like a low-gravity rocket booster where you press grab and propel yourself (slingshot) across the map at break-neck speeds, plus you can jump high or grapple hook or use a bow & arrow (sort of). There's a racing game, a game where you collect orbs, a game where you collect orbs but the floor is falling, and a bomb type game that I don't think works single-player.  \n\nGame is running on the Unity Engine. On my RTX 3080, I was getting mostly 72 fps. I did not experience any major issues or bugs. You have snap turning available. You can reset height, so you can technically play seated or standing (standing is easier though).\n\n[b]Rate ?/10.[/b]\n\n[quote]If you enjoyed my review, please consider joining my Steam Curator Group. You can join here: https://steamcommunity.com/groups/Oculus_WMR [/quote]",
